<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY C/A GAP WIDENS TO $501 MLN IN DEC 1996.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY C/A GAP WIDENS TO $501 MLN IN DEC 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's current account deficit</p>
<p>widened to $501 million in December 1996 from $53 million in</p>
<p>November, the National Bank of Hungary said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY CURRENT ACCOUNT, MONTH-ON-MONTH  ( millions)</p>
<p>				  DEC 96	 NOV 96	DEC 95</p>
<p> Current account	     -501	   -53	  -256</p>
<p> Trade balance		 -417	  -136	  -243</p>
<p>  Exports		     1,395	 1,283	 1,194</p>
<p>  Imports		     1,812	 1,419	 1,437</p>
<p> Services and incomes	-105	    34	   -65</p>
<p>  Tourism			  66	   128	    54</p>
<p>  Investments' income	-117	   -42	  -151</p>
<p>  Other current payments    -54	   -52	    31</p>
<p> Current transfers	     21	    50	    53</p>
<p>HUNGARY CURRENT ACCOUNT, ACCUMULATED ( millions)</p>
<p>			    JAN-DEC 96   JAN-DEC 95</p>
<p> Current account	   -1,678	-2,465</p>
<p> Trade balance	     -2,645	-2,436</p>
<p>  Exports		    14,183	12,853</p>
<p>  Imports		    16,828	15,290</p>
<p> Services and revenues	 45	 1,155</p>
<p>  Tourism		     1,288	   653</p>
<p> Investments' income     -1,433	-1,783</p>
<p> Other current payments     191	   -25</p>
<p> Current transfers	    922	 1,126</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
